# Provider dependencies via CLI setup

A library, generator, sample, or test does not gain a provider package to paper over a missing dialect, a compile error, or a failing test. `sqlite`, `mysql`, `postgres`, `sqlserver`, `oracle`, and every other catalog provider are installed by `npx @deterministic-code/datasources-cli setup` or `add`. The manifest lists only the providers that command wrote, matching `INSTALLED_PROVIDERS`.

Listing every provider in one package inflates the published bundle and makes CI compile every driver (`mysql_async`, `tokio-postgres`, bundled `rusqlite`) when the job never runs those engines.

Generators resolve a dialect from the provider catalog for a package the project already has. They do not depend on every driver.

```json
// ❌ BAD — every SQL provider added to fix a dialect lookup
{
  "dependencies": {
    "@deterministic-code/datasources-sqlite": "*",
    "@deterministic-code/datasources-mysql": "*",
    "@deterministic-code/datasources-postgres": "*",
    "@deterministic-code/datasources-sqlserver": "*",
    "@deterministic-code/datasources-oracle": "*"
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD — only the provider setup added
{
  "dependencies": {
    "@deterministic-code/datasources-sqlite": "*"
  }
}
```

```toml
# ❌ BAD
datasources-mysql = { path = "../providers/mysql" }
datasources-postgres = { path = "../providers/postgres" }
datasources-sqlite = { path = "../providers/sqlite" }

# ✅ GOOD
datasources-sqlite = { path = "../providers/sqlite" }
```
